<!--
    The four widget strings the snapshot cannot supply, in one of the app's languages.

    These follow the *system* locale rather than the app's, and that is right for what they are.
    Two are content descriptions, read aloud by TalkBack, which itself speaks the system language.
    The other two are what the widget says when there is no trustworthy snapshot — precisely the
    moments when the app's own language preference cannot be read. Every string that depends on
    diary content travels in the snapshot instead; see widget_habits.xml in values/.
-->
